{
  "prompt": "Improve the chess game to fix these critical issues:\n\n1. FIX WIN CONDITION - MOST IMPORTANT:\nRemove any win condition based on captured pieces or piece count.\nThe ONLY win condition is checkmate - when the king has no legal moves and is in check.\nAlso add stalemate detection - when a player has no legal moves but is NOT in check, it is a draw.\nRemove any code that declares winner based on missing pieces.\n\n2. FIX TIMERS:\n- Medium mode: 45 minutes per player (not per turn). Each player has their own clock that only counts down on their turn. Format as MM:SS. When time reaches 0:00 that player loses immediately with message \"Time's up! You lose.\"\n- Hard mode: 30 minutes per player. Same rules as medium but stricter.\n- When timer runs out do NOT restart it - show game over screen permanently.\n- Easy mode: no timer at all.\n\n3. ADD CHECK DETECTION:\n- After every move check if the opponent's king is in check\n- If in check: highlight the king's square in red, show \"⚠️ Check!\" warning in status bar\n- If in checkmate: show \"Checkmate! [color] wins!\" game over screen\n- A move is only legal if it does not leave your own king in check\n\n4. FIX GAME OVER SCREEN:\n- Remove the \"You Won!\" message that shows incorrectly at game start\n- Game over screen should only appear on: checkmate, stalemate, or timeout\n- Show a \"Play Again\" button that goes back to main menu\n- Show a \"Rematch\" button that restarts with same settings\n\n5. LEGAL MOVE VALIDATION:\n- A move is illegal if it leaves your own king in check\n- Filter out all such moves from valid moves list\n- This prevents players from making moves that expose their king\n\nKeep all multiplayer postMessage hooks intact.\nKeep receiveOpponentMove working correctly.\nKeep the menu screen with Easy/Medium/Hard levels.",
